        "digital_output",
        "pwm_output",
        "button"
      ],
      "notes": "Button A — onboard pushbutton, active-high (reads HIGH when pressed). Confirmed via the official Getting Started guide's hardware-overview page (\"Button A (GPIO 10)\") and the Arduino library's readButton()/buttonsInit() source (gpio_set_dir(GPIO_IN), no pull configured -> relies on the RP2040's power-on-reset default pull-down) cross-checked against the official MicroPython example treating a True/HIGH read as \"pressed\". Full digital_input/digital_output/pwm_output capability retained — ordinary GPIO wired to a switch to 3V3, not a dedicated/capacitive-only pin, matching this repo's vccgnd_yd_rp2040 PIN_USRKEY and adafruit_feather_scorpio PIN_BUTTON precedents."
    },
    {
      "name": "D11",
