      "name": "D21",
      "label": "GPIO21 (Led active high)",
      "codeName": "D21",
      "capabilities": [
        "digital_output",
        "pwm_output",
        "led_high"
      ],
      "notes": "PIN_LED / User LED — onboard single green status LED, active-high. Confirmed via the official Getting Started guide (\"Green user LED on pin 21\") and the Arduino library source's ledOn()/ledOff() (digitalWrite(21, HIGH)/digitalWrite(21, LOW) respectively). digital_input dropped to match this repo's established led_high precedent for dedicated onboard LED pins (rpipico, wiznet_5500_evb_pico, vccgnd_yd_rp2040, adafruit_feather_scorpio); pwm_output kept since arduino-pico's analogWrite() works on any RP2040 GPIO, enabling brightness dimming. No bus-alias collision found: this board's pins_arduino.h SPI0 (MISO 20/MOSI 19/SCK 18/SS 1), SPI1 (MISO 28/MOSI 27/SCK 26/SS 29), and Wire0/Wire1 (SDA 12/SCL 13, SDA 2/SCL 3) aliases none touch GPIO21, so no build_boards.js bus-capability auto-append contamination applies here (unlike adafruit_feather_scorpio's GPIO13/PIN_SPI0_SS case)."
    },
